{{- /*
musl-probe.tmpl — the ONLY definition of the host-libc probe.

Returns the string "true" on a musl Linux and "false" everywhere else. A
template returns a string, so every caller converts once, at the call site:

  {{- $isMuslLinux := eq (includeTemplate "musl-probe.tmpl" (dict "ctx" .)) "true" -}}

Input (dict):
  ctx  required; root chezmoi context (carries .chezmoi and any override key)

Resolution order:
  1. Not linux (ctx.chezmoi.os != "linux") -> "false". The override never
     applies off linux, because no other platform has a musl lock key.
  2. Override present -> its truthiness, with no subprocess. The key is
     `renderOverrides.muslLinux`; it is absent from .chezmoidata by design and
     exists only so a render can select the musl branch:

       chezmoi execute-template --override-data '{"renderOverrides":{"muslLinux":true}}'

     Both the JSON boolean true and the strings "true"/"1"/"yes" count as true.
  3. Otherwise -> the `ldd /bin/ls` probe, which is what a real apply runs.

Step 3 shells out through `output`, so `--override-data` cannot reach it; step 2
is the seam that lets CI render the `-musl` platform keys (bun, claude, mise,
agent-browser) without a musl runner (R28).
*/ -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" .) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "musl-probe.tmpl: expected a dict, got %s" (kindOf .)) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if not (hasKey . "ctx") -}}
{{-   fail "musl-probe.tmpl: ctx is required" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $ctx := .ctx -}}
{{- $isMuslLinux := false -}}
{{- if eq $ctx.chezmoi.os "linux" -}}
{{-   $override := "" -}}
{{-   $haveOverride := false -}}
{{-   if hasKey $ctx "renderOverrides" -}}
{{-     if hasKey $ctx.renderOverrides "muslLinux" -}}
{{-       $override = $ctx.renderOverrides.muslLinux -}}
{{-       $haveOverride = true -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   if $haveOverride -}}
{{-     if kindIs "bool" $override -}}
{{-       $isMuslLinux = $override -}}
{{-     else -}}
{{-       $isMuslLinux = has (lower (toString $override)) (list "true" "1" "yes") -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   else if eq (output "sh" "-c" "ldd /bin/ls 2>&1 | grep -q musl; echo $?" | trim) "0" -}}
{{-     $isMuslLinux = true -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $isMuslLinux | toString -}}
